# Copy to signing.local.env to sign and notarize `pnpm install:safari` builds
# with your own Developer ID. git ignores signing.local.env. Without it, builds
# are ad hoc signed and Safari needs "Allow unsigned extensions".
#
# List your certificates: security find-identity -v -p codesigning
# Use the SHA-1 hash (or the full name) of a "Developer ID Application"
# certificate, and its team ID (the code in brackets).
SIGN_IDENTITY=
TEAM_ID=
#
# Safari hides a Developer ID app until Apple notarizes it. Store your notary
# credentials in the keychain once (it asks for an app-specific password from
# account.apple.com), then put the profile name here:
#   xcrun notarytool store-credentials morning-tab-notary --apple-id YOUR_APPLE_ID --team-id YOUR_TEAM_ID
NOTARY_PROFILE=
